> End

Early on day 3, you and Eya set out from camp to see what this new land offers. A thin drizzle follows you out past the boats The camp has 7 food. That should last a little while She squints at the treeline. "New land," she says. "Watch what you eat, and watch what eats you." Where do you go first?
> Follow the stream inland

The stream The stream narrows between mossy stones, and small fish dart in the shallows. Further along, the water pools behind a low wall of woven branches. A weir, old but well made. Eya wades in without a second thought. "Just fish and sticks." Someone lived here once, and perhaps still does.
> Gather edible roots along the bank

You fill every basket and pouch you brought Eya grins and shoulders the load. "Now this is a land with something in it." You keep your distance from anything you cannot name.
> Head back to camp

The light grows long, and you and Eya turn back toward camp. Eya carries the food herself and refuses to let you help You carry nothing but your own thoughts.

You saw no one, but the land did not feel empty. Before you part, Eya asks what to make of tomorrow. What should Eya do tomorrow?
